 "text": "Sheridan County Nebraska\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nVirtual Nebraska\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's Office\nGIS Workshop\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nProperty Valuation Protests\nSpecial Licenses\nCounty Court Office\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict Court Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's Office\nSecretary of State\nLocal Election Results\nExtension\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nProbation\nPublic Defender\nPublic Transportation\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's Office\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's Exam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nGeneral Links\nOther Organizations\nWelcome\nNebraska County Websites\nSheridan County\nOur new website was brought online in May of 2019\nwith the help of MIPS Inc. MIPS Inc is the Technology Services\nDivision of the Nebraska Association of County Officials (NACO).\nNACO's website address is\nnebraskacounties.org\nSheridan Courthouse\nAddress\n301 E 2nd Street\nRushville, NE 69360\nHours\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nMonday - Thursday\n8:00 am - 1:00 pm\nFriday\nLocation\nLogin and Enroll\nGet the Mobile App\nOur online forms and documents are in PDF format.\nIf you do not have the latest Adobe's PDF reader installed, click on\nthe Adobe PDF image below.\nPublic Notices\nBoard of Commissioners\nMeeting Agenda\nBoard of Commissioners\nMeeting Minutes\nWe invite you to browse our web site to learn about the various\nCounty offices and the services Sheridan County, Nebraska offers its\ncitizens. Courthouse hours are from 8:00 - 4:30, Monday - Thursday\nand 8:00 - 1:00 on Friday, except on holidays.\nBy land area, Sheridan County is the fourth largest county in the\nState. It is 36 miles wide by 69 miles long. According to the U.S.\nCensus Bureau, the county has a total area of 2,470 square miles.\nThe population of Sheridan County in 2020 was 5127. The economy is\nprimarily Agricultural.\nThe southern portion is sandhills range land while the north\ncontains pine covered hills. The Mirage Flats Irrigation District\nsouth of Hay Springs is irrigated by water from the Box Butte\nReservoir. There is considerable farming, both dry land and pump\nirrigated, either side of US Highway 20.\nThere are four incorporated communities in Sheridan County. They\ninclude the County Seat of Rushville (population 816), Gordon\n(population 1504), Hay Springs (population 599), and Clinton\n(population 38). There are also five unincorporated villages within\nthe county's boundaries. They are Antioch, Bingham, Ellsworth,\nLakeside, and Whiteclay.\nCopyright © 2019 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
